CopyPasteBin Debian source package
==================================

This directory prepares the existing upstream tree as a non-native Debian
source package using the 3.0 (quilt) format and debhelper compatibility level
13. It builds three binary packages: the backend, GNOME Shell extension and
complete-installation metapackage. The final 1.2 source can be built locally
for artifact verification before a separately approved stable upload.

The binary packages deliberately contain no APT source configuration, signing
key, updater, maintainer script or per-user GNOME setting change. Repository
enrollment is a separate, explicit administrative action. Production signing
keys must never be stored in this source tree.

Run packaging/deb/build-source-package.sh from a Git checkout to export the
selected committed revision, add this debian directory and create an unsigned
source package under dist/source. The default is HEAD. CPB_DEB_SOURCE_REF may
select another explicit Git revision for an isolated experiment; the upstream
and Debian versions must still match.

The current final candidate targets Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute). Every upload must
use a version that has never previously been published to the selected
archive. Selecting a Launchpad archive, signing and uploading are deliberately
outside the local builder and require separate approval.
